# Git remotes

This checkout is a fork. Pushes, pull requests, and merges stay on the fork.

- `origin`: `https://github.com/ordinarylinuxuser/wayland-spice-clipboard-fix.git` — the only push target
- `upstream`: `https://github.com/chrisbelson/wayland-spice-clipboard-fix.git` — fetch only

Never push to `upstream` or to `chrisbelson/wayland-spice-clipboard-fix`. Do not open or merge pull requests against that repository.

```bash
git fetch upstream
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --repo ordinarylinuxuser/wayland-spice-clipboard-fix
```

```bash
# wrong: writes to the original repo
git push upstream HEAD
git push origin HEAD   # only if origin still points at chrisbelson
```
